<div class="examples u-grid gap-6">
<figure class="example @grid:col-span-6">
<p class="example-verdict example-verdict-dont">Don’t</p>
<div class="example-frame">
<div class="mailer-mock">
<p>Kensington Jewellery Repair</p>
<p class="text-heading">There’s an update on your job</p>
<p class="text-small">Sign in to see the latest on your repair.</p>
<p><span class="u-btn u-btn-primary">Sign in</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="example-caption example-caption-dont"><span>A vague heading and a button to find out more. Ana has to sign in to learn her ring is done, and the inbox preview tells her nothing.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure class="example @grid:col-span-6">
<p class="example-verdict example-verdict-do">Do</p>
<div class="example-frame">
<div class="mailer-mock">
<p>Kensington Jewellery Repair</p>
<p class="text-heading">Your ring is ready for pickup</p>
<dl class="u-dl">
<dt>Job</dt><dd class="u-data">#1042</dd>
<dt>To pay</dt><dd class="u-data">$85.00</dd>
<dt>Hours</dt><dd>Tuesday to Saturday, 10am to 7pm</dd>
</dl>
</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="example-caption example-caption-do"><span>The news in the heading, then what she needs at the counter. She can read it on the streetcar without opening anything else.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
